// An open connection to another program, over the network, plain or through TLS: Network
// receives what it sends, sends to it, and closes it, the same whichever it is. It's kept with the
// descriptor it's over, and whether what's received may be held where the descriptor being ready
// to read can't say: TLS's always may, as OpenSSL can hold what it's read, and the ssl package
// can't say whether it does.
external type Connection = "Unix.file_descr * (unit -> bool) * (unit -> (string, string) result) * (string -> (unit, string) result) * (unit -> unit)"
